Q: What is the difference between torch.no_grad() and torch.inference_mode()?

--- BASE: Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct ---
The context provided does not include any information about `torch.no_grad()` or `torch.inference_mode()`. Therefore, I cannot provide a reliable answer to your question based on the given information.

--- LORA: pytorch-rag ---
The documentation for [`torch.no_grad()`](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.no_grad.html) says:

> Disables gradient calculation.
>
> It will return a no-grad context manager which disables gradient calculation.

And for [`torch.inference_mode()`](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.inference_mode.html):

> Enables or disables inference mode (also see [Locally disabling inference mode](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/cuda.html#inference-mode)).

So both disable gradients but `no_grad` also disables autograd while `inference_mode` only disables autograd if CUDA is available.

